cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "manhattan-formalization: a Lean 4 formalization of The randomly oriented Manhattan lattice in 2D is transient"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper "The randomly
  oriented Manhattan lattice in 2D is transient" (Bou-Rabee and Peres): for
  almost every fair-coin orientation of the lines of Z^2, the quenched Green
  series of the walk is finite at every site (Theorem 1.1), deduced from a
  uniform bound on the Laplace transforms of the annealed continuous-time
  return probability (Theorem 1.2).  No result from the literature is assumed.
  The development contains no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - random walk in random environment
  - Manhattan lattice
  - transience
  - probability
license: Apache-2.0
# Add a Zenodo DOI and the repository URL here once an archived release is minted.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "The randomly oriented Manhattan lattice in 2D is transient"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bou-Rabee
        given-names: Ahmed
      - family-names: Peres
        given-names: Yuval
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.07621"
    notes: "The paper formalized by this repository; see paper/CHANGES_FROM_ARXIV.md for the text the formalization follows."
